// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_scene_twinkey_anchor.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: the ANCHOR half of the twin-key agreement — the property P3 Task 6's
// CAP_ANCHORS-implies-CAP_PER_LINE pin in `scene_caps()` exists to keep: an anchored
// scene raises $0008 and $0001 TOGETHER, from ONE field, so `parallax_mode_key()`'s
// CAP_ANCHORS gate is always lexically inside a live CAP_PER_LINE gate and
// tools/scene_spans.py's nesting-derived expectations stay sound.
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "back-door anchored scene folds to 9"
//
// ---- WHY THIS CASE ASSERTS THE FALSE HALF (the poison_scene_grid.emp inversion) ----
//
// The pin ITSELF cannot be driven red by any input, and that is a MEASURED property,
// not a guess: both bits derive from the same `sc_anchor` field through the same
// `scene_anchor_ch()` accessor — arm 2 of `scene_forces_per_line()` and `scene_caps()`'s
// `anchored` fold are the SAME `!= $FF` predicate on the SAME payload — so no authored
// value, `Scene{ .. }` back door included, can raise one without the other (probed
// 2026-08-22: this exact fixture, asserted == $0008, fired "folds to 9"; asserted
// == $0009, built clean). Its red-first evidence is Task 6's arm-neutering (caps 12 on
// both anchored scenes, recorded at the ensure), and the residual exposure — a game
// declaring SCANLINE_CAPS by hand rather than from fold_caps() — is booked in the plan's
// Task 15 DONE block. Writing a "poison" that pretended to reach the pin would be the
// faked-poison anti-pattern Task 14 named.
//
// What CAN be witnessed from the input side — permanently, in the lane's only verb —
// is the agreement itself: the fixture is the documented `Scene{ .. }` back door (the
// one construction that skips every scene() guard, so nothing softens the question)
// carrying an anchor and NOTHING else live, and the ensure asserts its fold is $0008,
// CAP_ANCHORS alone. That is false by exactly ONE BIT — the $0001 under test — so the
// diagnostic the lane captures, quoting the fold value 9, is the PROOF the two bits
// still rise together. A CLEAN build here is the regression: it would mean an anchored
// input really can fold to $0008 alone, the desync the pin exists to make impossible.
// A fold of anything else (the fragment's "9" missing) fails the case too.
//
// Expected `[Error]` count is 1: the back-door scene is otherwise empty (locked plane,
// one pad "layer", no tables, no curve, no v-deform, Undeclared policy with no subject),
// so no constructor guard runs — the back door skips scene() — and no scene_caps() pin
// fires at caps $0009. A count of 2 means a fold pin started firing on a plain anchored
// scene, which would be the agreement breaking somewhere ELSE in the fold.
//
// THE GLOB IMPORTS ARE THE AUTHOR'S OWN SPELLING — see poison_scene_grid.emp's header.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_scene_twinkey_anchor

use engine.level.scene_dsl.*
use engine.level.parallax_dsl.*

const POISON_TKA_PADS: [SceneLayer; 8] = [
    no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
    no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
]

// The documented Scene{ .. } back door: an anchored scene with nothing else live.
// Anchor shifts both 15 (no deform), channel 0. sc_count 1 over a pad layer keeps every
// fold walk trivially clean (world_y 0, locked plane: plane line 0, on-grid).
const POISON_TKA_SCENE: Scene = Scene{
    sc_layers:             POISON_TKA_PADS,
    sc_count:              1,
    sc_v_factor:           15,
    sc_v_center:           0,
    sc_v_offset:           0,
    sc_v_factor_fg:        0,
    sc_deform_fg:          SceneDeform.None,
    sc_deform_bg:          SceneDeform.None,
    sc_v_deform:           SceneVDeform.None,
    sc_anchor:             SceneAnchor.At(0, 15, 15),
    sc_left_col_mask:      SceneLeftColMask.Undeclared,
    sc_precision:          0,
    sc_transition:         0,
    sc_pad_5D:             default,
    sc_mask_raw:           -1,
    sc_v_deform_shift_raw: -1,
}

const POISON_TKA_CAPS = scene_caps(POISON_TKA_SCENE)

// ---- THE FALSE HALF — THIS DIAGNOSTIC IS THE PROOF, NOT THE PROBLEM ----
ensure(POISON_TKA_CAPS == $0008,
       "poison_scene_twinkey_anchor: back-door anchored scene folds to {POISON_TKA_CAPS}, not $0008 alone — CAP_ANCHORS ($0008) and CAP_PER_LINE ($0001) rose TOGETHER from the one sc_anchor field, which is the twin-key agreement doing its job. THE LANE REQUIRES THIS DIAGNOSTIC. A clean build here is the regression: an anchored input folding to $0008 alone would put parallax_mode_key()'s anchor gate inside an elided per-line gate and hand tools/scene_spans.py an expectation from a build where the whole site is gone")
